# Listening Notes — required environment variables.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values. Nothing here is secret;
# it is the list of what a copy needs, so it lives in the repo. .env.local is
# gitignored and never leaves your machine.
#
# On Vercel these go in Project → Settings → Environment Variables instead.
#
# Editing .env.local: use a terminal, not VS Code. VS Code silently fails to
# save dotfiles in this project. Check your work with `cat .env.local`.

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Neon Postgres connection string.
# Neon dashboard → your project → Connection Details → "Connection string".
# Include ?sslmode=require.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require

# Signs the login cookie. Any long random string — 32+ characters.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Changing it retires every session cookie issued under the old one, so you are
# signed out on every device and log in again with the same password. That is
# the whole cost — disruptive, not dangerous. Don't rotate it casually; do
# rotate it if you think it leaked. Being signed out afterwards is the expected
# outcome, not a fault.
SESSION_SECRET=

# The password you type to reach the writing side of your own journal.
# There is no account and no username; this is the whole of the lock.
SESSION_PASSWORD=

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Claude API key, for album research and the listening companion.
# console.anthropic.com → API keys.
#
# Billing note: this draws on your Console API credit balance, which is a
# SEPARATE pool from a Claude.ai subscription. A "credit balance too low"
# error means the API balance, not the subscription.
#
# Leave blank and the journal works; the AI features are simply absent.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Last.fm API key, for the "now playing" beacon.
# last.fm/api/account/create — read-only, free, takes about a minute.
#
# Get your own rather than borrowing one. The key identifies the *application*,
# not the listener, so every copy sharing a key also shares one rate limit —
# somebody else's busy journal would throttle yours.
#
# Read only on the server, by /api/public/beacon, and never sent to the
# browser. The listener's username is a separate thing and lives in the
# settings table, not here.
#
# Leave blank and the beacon simply does not appear.
LASTFM_KEY=
